      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5f7129762031a358a533d358",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Judging by what you and others who replied are saying, what you are experiencing is very likely audio decompression when loading audio assets on avatars. I wrote a (probably over-detailed) post about it not too long ago. To summarize, Unity's default behavior of loading audio assets is to decompress them on the main thread (the thread the game logic runs on) before sending them to memory. While this is happening, everything else on that thread must wait for the decompression to finish. Changing a single setting in the import settings of audio assets fixes this.\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/smoother-way-of-handling-audio-asset-loading-to-fix-the-freezes-when-loading-in",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
